Z||000005||pherder||12-02-2001||04:47 PM||||How about this from one of the Fiero lists ...<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Us: Stickers for contingency.<BR>Them: Stickers for horsepower.<P>Us: Boost guage on a blown car, nitrous guage on a squeezed car.<BR>Them: Both guages on a normally aspirated car.<P>Us: 500 lb-ft of torque at 3,500 rpm<BR>Them: 50 lb-ft of tourque at 35,000rpm<P>Us: Headers and 3" exhaust<BR>Them: Stock pea shooter exhast pipe w/ 5" tip.<P>Us: Showing off a 500 hp dyno sheet.<BR>Them: Boasting that their 150 hp mill makes more hp / liter.<P>Us: Installing subframe connectors to stiffen the chassis.<BR>Them: Connecting the subframes w/ neon lights.<P>Us: Keeping a low profile and letting e.t.'s tell the story.<BR>Them: Hoping the outragous body kit will distract anyone from discussing<BR>e.t.'s.<P>Us: Installing a 12 point cage after breaking into the 11's.<BR>Them: Installing a 12 point cage for more places to mount gauges.<P>Us: Felling the car shake from a lumpy cam.<BR>Them: Felling the car shake from booming bass.<P>Us: Comfy stock bucket seats on a 9 second street car.<BR>Them: Back breaking fiberglass racing buckets on a 17 second street car.<P>Us: Sideways in 3rd gear.<BR>Them: Sideways to avoid high centering on a speed bump.<P>Us: Cruising and burnout contest at car shows.<BR>Them: Dancing and stereo competitions at car shows.<P>Us: 600hp makes for an earth shaking street car.<BR>Them: 600 watts per channel makes for an ear shattering street car.<P>Us: Buying an aftermarket shifter for shorter throws.<BR>Them: Buying an aftermarket shifter for the lighted knob.<P>The best one for Us here @ LS1.com<BR>Us: Spending $2,000.00 to get a new Z28 in the 11's.<BR>Them: Spending $10,000.00 to get a Civic into the 12's.<P>They do clarify that they have the upmost respect for anyone driving a serious<BR>built import such as a modded Supra (except green ones) or RX7, this is aimed<BR>at the posers.<P><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||3
