Z||000008||lou||12-02-2001||05:33 PM||||Lets face face it american cars give you more bang for the buck, you can buy a used 5.7 L Camaro for under $7500 that will blow the doors off any used $15000 import and everyone knows you have a muscle car.  With imports you have to advertise that the miniscule engine that came in your car has been HIGHLY modified to try to compete with a real muscle car.  On the street it is torque that wins races, on the track its brute horsepower. You can't get either from a small engine without spending a fortune and making it unreliable.  Lucky for import car owners that the Camaro and Firebird have gone the way of the Fiero, now all they have to worry aobut is Mustangs, Corvettes and Vipers.  Don't forget it was America that invented the muscle car and there are no substitutes for the real thing.||||reg||1
