Z||000023||rx7speed||12-02-2001||07:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou:<BR><B>Lets face face it american cars give you more bang for the buck, you can buy a used 5.7 L Camaro for under $7500 that will blow the doors off any used $15000 import and everyone knows you have a muscle car.  With imports you have to advertise that the miniscule engine that came in your car has been HIGHLY modified to try to compete with a real muscle car.  On the street it is torque that wins races, on the track its brute horsepower. You can't get either from a small engine without spending a fortune and making it unreliable.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>ok well here goes your theory<BR>I spent 2200 for my car it was a 87 rx7<BR>spent about 1200 to get a stock turbo motor in there. maybe put another 300 for the exhaust and intercooler and all the pipes I needed for that. then throw in a boost controler and FCD so I dont run lean and my total including the car is at about $4000<BR>3k less then your 5.7 camaro and I was able to run a G-tech time of 12.5 with 0-60 in 4.5<BR>the car is very reliable. my only problem is I am using the rest of the N/A driveline so I did break a driveshaft once. no big deal<P>and yes I know a g-tech is not the best way to tell how fast you are running but I dont think it would be that far off.<P>soon here I should have a few other goodies that might throw in another 1500 and I would still be below your 7000 camaro and I should hit high 10 to low 11 if not better<BR>so bang for the buck is not always american V8<P>and am I highly modified? unless you want to call what few mods I have highly then I woud not say so. the motor is stock from a Turbo rx7 so is the turbo. the only thing I have done is use slightly larger injectors and an intercooler and a few electonics to help me boost higher and safe.<P>oh and as for torque I am only hitting about 295hp and maybe 250-280 ft/lbs so you guys have more the v8 camaro has more then me why can't it pull my times?<P><BR>dont mean to be a prick but american is not the only way or always the best way to go<P>I agree that there is a lot of rice out there though that puts a sticker on there ****  and thinks it is all fast now and that stuff needs to end but dont put us all in that boat.<P>and htanx pherder that did give me a laugh since I do see a lot of rice boys over here that do the same thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>who needs pistons I have rotary<P>||||reg||1
