Z||000028||FieroMaster88||12-02-2001||08:18 PM||||I am with Jaei Sun on this issue.  The hot rod market lately has gone towards small engine performance.  Honda, Mitsubishi, Nissan, Toyota all see this, and build cars  that can easily be made fast or already are fast.   <P>Honda has the Civic, which sure everyone has, but it has a solid power plant with lots of upgradability.  They are in a price range that younger people can afford, which makes them popular.  Honda also has the Prelude.  Very nice car, rather quick with Vtec and has a lot of upgradability options too.  The American part of Honda, Acura, has the Integra.  The Type R integra comes stock with 200HP.  I have 2 friends with these cars and man are they fast.  With the 1.8L DOHC VTEC  engine mated with the 5 speed Trans they get up and go.  Very nice and they have many many upgrades available!<P>Nissan also have cars that can be modified easily.  They have the Maxima.  Nice car, little on the expensive side, but they have upgrade's available.  The best Nissan car out there is the 300Z.  Get the Twin Turbo option and who needs upgrades?<P>Mitsubishi had some really sporty cars, too bad they candled most of them.  The GSX Eclipse came with AWD and a 2.0L DOHC Turbo which put out 210HP from the factory.  Very fast, Very fun!  I can only hope they bring the Lancer EVO to the states sometime soon!<P>Toyota has the Celica.  I don't remember the engine that comes in them or the HP right now.  Nice car, have seen more and more upgrades coming along for these lately.   They also have the Supra.  I have dyno vids of these producing 800+HP at the rear wheel's!  Amazing!<P>I forgot to mention Subaru, who have the WRX Impreza.  AWD Turbo car with 224 HP from the factory.  Fun sporty car with lots of mod's available.    Also Mazda with their RX7.  Twin Turbocharger rotary engine which if I remember right has a 1.3L with 255 hp.   That's amazing! <P>Now what American automotive manufactories make cars that compete with these?!?! GM (my favorite auto manufactory) have the Cavalier and the sunfire....not really much there even with the 2.4L.  The 2.2's are dogs even with a 5 speed.  <P>Ford doesn't have anything that really competes with them.  They have the stang...but the type R integra will beat a GT stang...and the stang has 4 more cylinder's.  <P>And dodge has the neon.  They have the SOHC 2.0L which is also a dog.  <P>If I had my choice I would choose American, well, I did choose American!  But if I wanted a small economy sport car that I could modify to go faster I would have to choose Rice.  More options to go faster and more reliable performance.<P>Wow..what a book that turned out to be.  GO ahead, flame me.  I don't care.  If you all want to be shallow minded and bash me because you cant see the truth, so be it.  I hope it makes you feel better.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Good day! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
