Z||000036||yo_sweet||12-02-2001||11:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sloth85GT:<BR><B> Ummmm my stock 85GT has beaten a Beretta GTZ.....and when I get the LT1 in it, the car will be worth under $10,000 and pound the doors off of a $40,000 (or whatever amount of money those guys waste on it) Integra Type R. It's just a matter of power per dollar. I hate hondas with a passion, maybe that opinion could have been different if so many ricers didn't have to ruin it by going for upgrading the body and looks before even touching the engine. This has also been done to a Fiero, that guy with the black GT with that UGLY carbon fiber wing and the DVD player. I asked him what his enging mods are, he said it's stock.....What's up with that? My paint sucks, I don't have much money, but what little money I DO have, will go to performance before looks. AFTER the LT1, I will shoot some paint on her. I don't have to make my Fiero look like something it's not. If guys like Civics so much, then why change to body so much that you can't even tell what it is? I would like imports more if they weren't always riced. And rice doesn't make sense to me....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>you may have beaten him off the line but he would smoke you in the long run , besides you could prolbibly take a type r off the line, maybe you raceda  z26 berettea 3.1L<P><P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
