Z||000038||Spektrum-87GT||12-02-2001||11:54 PM||||pro drivers can barely break the type r into the 6's, and thats after a long smokey burnout and taking the rpms up to 6k rpms and dropping the clutch... find a ricer that can do that. besides, who do you know with a REAL type r that rices it... not too many. its those ugly pos integra ls's or whatever the hell they are that are so pathetic. my first rice kill was a red one, wasnt even a race, and he thought he could take me... kinda shows you the attitude of the ricers.||||reg||1
Z||000039||Spektrum-87GT||12-02-2001||11:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sloth85GT:<BR><B> I don't have to make my Fiero look like something it's not. If guys like Civics so much, then why change to body so much that you can't even tell what it is? I would like imports more if they weren't always riced. And rice doesn't make sense to me....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>its fiero owners like this... that make me proud to be part of this community... you rock sloth!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000040||SCCA FIERO||12-02-2001||11:58 PM||||About that Integra Type R. I think those cars cost around $25k? My little 88 Fiero Coupe with no mods other than a stock 2.8 V6 and poly bushings beat it on the track (that's where it counts, right?) and the Type R had 2 different drivers in at least 2 different events. I beat their time every run (I think every run, not exactly sure, but if you doubt me, I can find the link for the posted times). I think I have around $4,000 in my Fiero including the price of the tank of gas that was in it.<P>And that AWD GSX Talon. They run around $25k or so? Maybe more? Well, on the autocross course it's not that great. The little punk laughed when I answered his question, "How much horsepower does that thing make?" He didn't seem to think it was funny when I compared our first run times, or the second run, or the third or fourth.<P>Not trying to add fuel to the fire, but I am proud to be an American. Proud to drive my American Piece of **** , too!!||||reg||1
Z||000041||FieroMaster88||12-03-2001||12:07 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>pro drivers can barely break the type r into the 6's, and thats after a long smokey burnout and taking the rpms up to 6k rpms and dropping the clutch... find a ricer that can do that. besides, who do you know with a REAL type r that rices it... not too many. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>6's with a long smokey burn out is good.  If it runs 6's with tons of tire spin..imagine what it would do with <B>NO</B> tire spin!  <P>My friend Ed Sackley autox's his type R.  Has a full exhaust system and racing suspension setup.  As he says "I bought the car to have fun, so thats what I am gonna do!"  <P>SCCA Fiero:  Are you SERIOUS?!?!  You beat the Type R on the track in a 88 coupe with a v6 and a 5 speed?!?!  Thats great!  They give me hell about my car all the time and about how "crappy" they handle.  I guess I will have to go to the track with them next year then..... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>GSX Eclipses run about $15K to $20K with low miles.  They are good straight line cars, but they are heavy.  Kinda their down side.  I still like them though.  Never said I would trade my car for any of these.  I just think they are nice too.  If I wanted one I would have purchased one instead of my Fiero!  Not trying to start any wars either.  I guess I dont hate any cars, just stupid people!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by FieroMaster88 (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000042||SS_304||12-03-2001||12:48 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I hate hondas with a passion, maybe that opinion could have been different if so many ricers didn't have to ruin it by going for upgrading the body and looks before even touching the engine. This has also been done to a Fiero, that guy with the black GT with that UGLY carbon fiber wing and the DVD player. I asked him what his enging mods are, he said it's stock.....What's up with that? My paint sucks, I don't have much money, but what little money I DO have, will go to performance before looks. AFTER the LT1, I will shoot some paint on her. I don't have to make my Fiero look like something it's not. If guys like Civics so much, then why change to body so much that you can't even tell what it is? I would like imports more if they weren't always riced. And rice doesn't make sense to me....<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I own a white '91 Honda Civic CRX HF (62 HP, Honda's sailship for "THE" economy car before the Insight), and I've been saving up for modifications since I got a job at the same time I got the car.<P>Don't assume that every teenager on the street with a Civic are going to rice them up -- I could blow all my money on a body kit, new muffler (more known as fart cans), spoiler, rims, ... "TYPE R" logos, the works. Just head over to my local Car Boutique shop and it'd all be done.<P>No.<P>My CRX, at the moment, has EVERYTHING stock with no performance modifications except for the air filter intake tube and resonator, in which I took out for better low-end torque (hey, 62 HP!! I need all I can get for now).<P>And I plan to keep it that way -- except for new wheels ... my wheels are rather rusty and missing the honda "H" emblems, I want to buy the same set, only new.<P>I love the stock love of my CRX; it's my favourite design next to the Fiero.<P>With my saved-up money, I'll buy a 130 HP ZC DOHC engine, throw it in there, buy a new exhaust system (GReddy, so no fart can, quality stuff here) since my muffler is AWOL, and generally do a little more I/H/E. It'll be a sleeper, and I'll leave the "HF" logo, proudly, on.<P>I hate ricers with a passion, and I hate it when others attempt to race me JUST because I drive a CRX (the VERY car which started off the import/rice-car scene in the first place). <P>I have friends at school who are complently into this rice-boy trend. They've tried to get me to get a body kit, stickers, lights, etc. (One of them stole a lot of ****  from Car Boutique, don't ask me how, and wants to give some ricey stuff to me for my car). When I told one of them about my plan, why I had gotten a HF (it's lighter than the Si model, the 130 HP engine I'm planning is 20 HP more powerful than the Si engine), he blew me off just because it wasn't a Si. <P>Those who rice-up their cars entirely for looks are not actually car enthusiants -- they're all cashing it for the materialistic value and for looking "cool." Like that guy who lambasted me because my CRX wasn't a Si.<P>As much as I hate this current trend, it'll eventually blow over, just like the muscle car trend did a long, long time ago   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by SS_304 (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000043||NOCONES||12-03-2001||12:55 AM||||A eclipse GSX with a good driver on autocross tires sould decimate a fiero.. flat out anihilate it.  they have close to 220hp.. tons and tons of grip.. the 1st gen's don't wiegh too much &lt;3400 i think.. and handle really well..<BR>there was one that ran local where i live that was only beaten by an 95RX-7 turbo on racing tires with the best driver i've ever seen...  and i was only 3 seconds behind them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> on street tires<P>------------------<BR>NOCONES<BR>-84 2M4 <BR>-4.10 4-speed<BR>-SCCA sollo II <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nocones_1.jpg"> <P>Addmit it... it's just as much fun alone...  Solo II||||reg||1
Z||000044||artherd||12-03-2001||04:21 AM||||James? are your friends on crack?  (You simply can NOT beat mid-engine handling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I doubt that with a set of springs and 17s that their cars could pull over one static Gee.<P>FWD cars get crap for launch, you're right, 6s are frigging amazing!!  From a 30mph roll the story would be different...<P>Every car to me has it's own charm, I'm even warming to civics in a way (they have a decent multilink suspension in a 'cheap rotton wood struts should be fine' market. at least, they used to...)<P>The world's a big and fantastically intresting place, there's room enough for all of us and our cars.<P>I find that when I look for the posative things in other enthusiests, instead of negative, that I end up meeting other cool car dudes. Peroid.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>  <BR>6's with a long smokey burn out is good.  If it runs 6's with tons of tire spin..imagine what it would do with [b]NO</B> tire spin!  <P>My friend Ed Sackley autox's his type R.  Has a full exhaust system and racing suspension setup.  As he says "I bought the car to have fun, so thats what I am gonna do!"  <P>SCCA Fiero:  Are you SERIOUS?!?!  You beat the Type R on the track in a 88 coupe with a v6 and a 5 speed?!?!  Thats great!  They give me hell about my car all the time and about how "crappy" they handle.  I guess I will have to go to the track with them next year then.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>GSX Eclipses run about $15K to $20K with low miles.  They are good straight line cars, but they are heavy.  Kinda their down side.  I still like them though.  Never said I would trade my car for any of these.  I just think they are nice too.  If I wanted one I would have purchased one instead of my Fiero!  Not trying to start any wars either.  I guess I dont hate any cars, just stupid people!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by FieroMaster88 (edited 12-03-2001).][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
